unner.adapter`, `model.selfDeclared`;\n47:`trace.json` for the timeline so far). The runner writes\n48-`journal/<date>/trace.json` from the agent CLI's own event stream after\n49-every phase call — tool calls, tokens, cost as the CLI reported it or an\n50-estimate from `pipeline/config.json` `pricing` (dated). In the ship phase,\n51:copy it into `WHY.timeline`:\n52-\n53-```\n54:node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/<date>/trace.json\n55-```\n56-\n57-The build (`tools/check-why.mjs`) refuses a placeholder, non-ASCII copy, a\n58-bad URL, a `day`/`date`/`agent`/`model` that disagrees with the journal, a\n59:timeline that disagrees with the trace, or a tutorial that does not render\n60-as those six steps. The critic scores whether the pages tell the truth.\n61-Budget: 1-3 paragraphs of at most 320 characters per page — it is\n62-orientation; the detail is the journal.\n63-\n64-## Rules that fail silently\n65-\n66-- **`ctx.target`, never `ctx.output`** — they agree until the template renders nested.\n67-- **Never guess a `flattenedStableKey`** — compute it with `findStableKeys`. A wrong key renders *silently black* and exits 0.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PpfKrEYACwuwymfxhtY3YR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
